### Resolved: recurring "stale registration" -> ROOT CAUSE was a build timestamp
`test_registration_guard.sh` kept FAILING after every vsim rebuild. Root cause
(found after an initial wrong guess that config.inc had no volatile content):
**config.inc line 1 is `// created on <date>` -- a build timestamp** -- so
hashing it RAW changes the identity on every rebuild even when the config is
byte-identical otherwise. Every rebuild self-staled the registration.

Proper fix (not a rename-whack-a-mole): the guard now hashes config.inc with the
`^// created on ` line STRIPPED (`test_registration_guard.sh`), and the
`engine.env` recompute instruction matches. The normalized hash is stable across
rebuilds. Verified: CSR set (manifest cols 1-9) BYTE-IDENTICAL across rebuilds;
cold-cache `--verify` re-proven on both rebuilt binaries (premium 147 / advanced
148 fields, clean sweep); dirs re-registered to the stable hashes
(`ax45mpv_premium-5bea8bdc`, `ax46mpv_advanced-a13f86a3`). Guard + all four
engine tests green, and they STAY green across future rebuilds.
